## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical crypto for multi-tenant KCNA: encryption at rest, per-tenant keys, rotation, and in-flight re-encryption.

## Key Concepts

- Envelope encryption
- Per-tenant DEKs
- KMS master key
- Rotation workflow
- Least privilege and auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-encryption flow for a tenant payload
function encryptPayload(tenantId, payload, dekStore, kms) {
  const dek = dekStore.getDEK(tenantId);
  const wrapped = kms.wrapKey(dek);
  const iv = crypto.randomBytes(12);
  const cipher = crypto.createCipheriv('aes-256-gcm', dek, iv);
  // ... encryption steps
  return { ciphertext, dekWrapped: wrapped };
}
```

